  "id": "fibromyalgia",
  "term": "fibromyalgia",
  "definition": "Fibromyalgia is a common rheumatic condition affecting tissues outside the joints, marked by widespread muscle pain and multiple tender spots in the muscles. The pain often worsens with inactivity or cold and is often accompanied by sleep problems, fatigue, stiffness, headaches, and sometimes depression.",
